r over its heads rate is Beta(kappa s,\nkappa (1 - s)) with the concentration kappa fitted (kappa = 2 recovers the\nincumbent's Beta(2 s, 2 (1 - s))). Large kappa: people picture trick coins as\nonly mildly rigged, so a modest heads/tails imbalance is weak evidence against\nchance; small kappa: they picture grossly rigged coins. Addresses the critique\nthat among length-8 pairs where the more-switching sequence is the more\nlopsided, people choose the more-switching sequence more often than predicted\n(balance weighed less against switching than the flat prior implies).\n\nDescription of the refined model follows.\n\n'''\nsrc=src.replace('\"\"\"Gambler\\'s run-length belief', head+\"Gambler's run-length belief\",1)\nold='''    a_h = 2.0 * s_heads\n    a_t = 2.0 - a_h\n    seq_lbias = (\n        pt.gammaln(seq_heads + a_h) + pt.gammaln(seq_len - seq_heads + a_t)\n        - pt.gammaln(seq_len + 2.0)\n        - pt.gammaln(a_h) - pt.gammaln(a_t) + math.lgamma(2.0)\n    )'''\nnew='''    # Fitted concentration of the rigging prior (kappa = 2: the incumbent's).\n    log_kappa = pm.Normal(\"log_kappa\", mu=math.log(2.0), sigma=1.0)\n    kappa = pm.Deterministic(\"kappa\", pt.exp(log_kappa))\n    a_h = kappa * s_heads\n    a_t = kappa - a_h\n    seq_lbias = (\n        pt.gammaln(seq_heads + a_h) + pt.gammaln(seq_len - seq_heads + a_t)\n        - pt.gammaln(seq_len + kappa)\n        - pt.gammaln(a_h) - pt.gammaln(a_t) + pt.gammaln(kappa)\n    )'''\nassert old in src\nsrc=src.replace(old,new)\nopen(sys.argv[2],'w').write(src)\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && timeout 1500 /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_d